# Accepted image-scan findings. Each entry names why it is accepted and what
# removes it. An entry with no reason does not belong in this file.

# Spring Framework 6.2.19 - three advisories published 2026-08-20. There is no
# open-source fix on the 6.2 line: Spring's own advisories list 6.2.20 as
# Enterprise Support Only, and the fixed open-source version is 7.0.9, which
# requires Spring Boot 4 (Framework 7, Tomcat 11). Boot 3.5 is the supported
# platform of this tree and a Boot 4 migration is tracked as open work in
# docs/architecture/19-implementation-phases.md §19.2 and §19.6.
#
# Reachability evidence, checked in this tree (backend/*/src/main):
#   CVE-2026-47884 (spring-webmvc, XsltView SSRF/RCE, needs XsltView and an
#     "/**" mapping that falls through to view rendering): no XsltView, no
#     TransformerFactory, no .xsl anywhere; every controller is a
#     @RestController answering JSON. Not reachable.
#   CVE-2026-47890 (spring-webmvc + spring-webflux, SSE stream corruption with
#     view fragments, needs Server-Sent Events carrying view fragments): no SSE
#     - no ServerSentEvent, no text/event-stream, no SseEmitter. Not reachable.
#   CVE-2026-47892 (spring-webflux, header predicate bypass in functional
#     endpoints, needs RouterFunction-style endpoints guarded by header
#     predicates): no RouterFunction anywhere; WebFlux is present only for
#     WebClient in the webhook transport, which carries no endpoint routing.
#     Not reachable.
#
# These three entries are REMOVED when the tree runs on Spring Boot 4 /
# Framework 7.0.9 or later. If any of the three features above ever enters the
# codebase before that migration, this file is wrong and the finding is live.
CVE-2026-47884
CVE-2026-47890
CVE-2026-47892
